        <li><strong>Autonomous Mobility Solutions:</strong> Develop wearable navigation aids that communicate directly with smart city infrastructure to guide users safely, bypassing obstacles in real-time.</li>
        <li><strong>Inclusive Design Protocols:</strong> Establish new industry standards where accessibility is integrated from the first line of code, rather than added as an afterthought.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Methodology and the Role of Oversight</h2>
    <p>To ensure ethical rigor and community trust, the project will be governed by an independent ethics board. This board will include representatives from the disability community and technical experts. A key part of our oversight framework involves the <span class="keynote">constable</span> of the ethics committee—a role specifically designated to monitor data privacy and algorithmic bias. This figure will act as a guardian of the community's rights, ensuring that every algorithm deployed respects individual autonomy and dignity.</p>

    <h2>Expected Impact</h2>
    <p>By implementing these systems, we anticipate a significant reduction in social isolation and a marked increase in independent living for millions of people. The ultimate goal is to transform the narrative of disability from one of limitation to one of empowered capability, where technology acts as a bridge rather than a barrier.</p>

